out preparation.  \n- **K: e8-d7**: King walk? Too dangerous early; no reason to expose the king.  \n- **R: a8-b8 / R: h8-g8**: Rook moves seem passive or premature.\n\nThe most forcing and advantageous move is **N: c6-e5**, attacking the undefended white knight on g5. White has no immediate way to protect it, so Black will likely win a piece (knight) for free next move.\n\nReason:  \n**N: c6-e5** wins material by attacking the unprotected white knight on g5. It’s a simple and effective move that increases pressure immediately. No other move offers such a direct gain.\n\nAnswer: N: c6-e5"}
